# FYPMS — Final Year Project Management System

A full-stack web application for managing final year projects in an academic setting. The system supports three roles — **Admin**, **Supervisor**, and **Student** — each with tailored dashboards for project creation, task tracking, meeting scheduling, and AI-assisted feedback.

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer      | Technology                                                    |
|------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|
| Frontend   | React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Material UI 7, TanStack Query     |
| Backend    | ASP.NET Core Web API (.NET 10), Entity Framework Core         |
| Database   | PostgreSQL (via Npgsql)                                       |
| Cache      | Redis                                                         |
| AI         | Google Gemini (via `Google.GenAI`) for automated feedback     |
| Scheduling | FullCalendar                                                  |
| PDF/Excel  | QuestPDF, ClosedXML                                           |
| Auth       | JWT (Bearer tokens) with BCrypt password hashing              |
| Testing    | Playwright (end-to-end)                                       |
| DevOps     | Docker + Docker Compose                                       |

---

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- [Docker Desktop](https://www.docker.com/products/docker-desktop/) (or Docker Engine + Docker Compose)
- An `.env` file at `PMS/.env` with the following variables:

```
MAIL_ACCOUNT=your-email@example.com
MAIL_PASSWORD=your-app-password
JWT_SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
```

> **Note:** Email functionality is disabled by default (`DISABLE_MAIL=true` in `docker-compose.yaml`). Remove or set to `false` to enable.

### Running the Application

```sh
cd PMS
docker compose up --build
```

Once all services are healthy, open **http://localhost:3000** in your browser.

### Services & Ports

| Service       | Container           | Port  |
|---------------|---------------------|-------|
| React Client  | `react_pms`         | 3000  |
| .NET Server   | `dotnet_server`     | 5081  |
| PostgreSQL    | `postgres_db_pms`   | 5431  |
| Redis         | `redis_pms`         | 6379  |

---

## Test Credentials

| Role       | Email                | Password   |
|------------|----------------------|------------|
| Student    | student@uni.com      | password   |
| Supervisor | supervisor@uni.com   | password   |

> Admin accounts are created via database seeding — refer to the project setup guide for the admin password.

---

## Features

- **Admin dashboard** — Create/manage projects and user accounts
- **Supervisor dashboard** — Oversee assigned projects, create tasks, define grading criteria, schedule meetings
- **Student dashboard** — View tasks, submit deliverables, receive AI-generated feedback, book supervisor meetings
- **AI feedback** — Gemini-powered automatic feedback on student submissions
- **Scheduler** — Bookable meeting slots with FullCalendar integration
- **Progress reports** — Exportable as PDF
- **Email notifications & reminders** — Configurable via environment variables

---

## Project Structure

```
PMS/
├── client/                  # React + TypeScript + Vite frontend
│   └── src/
│       ├── components/      # Reusable UI components by feature
│       ├── routes/          # Page-level route components (admin / normal)
│       ├── providers/       # Auth context provider
│       └── lib/             # Shared types, config, theme
├── server/                  # ASP.NET Core Web API backend
│   └── src/
│       ├── Controllers/     # REST API endpoints
│       ├── Services/        # Business logic layer
│       ├── Models/          # Entity Framework domain models
│       ├── DTOs/            # Data Transfer Objects
│       └── Lib/             # Utilities (AI, JWT, RBAC, PDF, Mail)
├── tests/                   # Playwright end-to-end tests
├── docker-compose.yaml      # Docker orchestration
└── docker-compose.test.yaml # Test environment orchestration
```

---

## Testing

The project includes **Playwright** end-to-end tests located in `PMS/tests/`.

```sh
cd PMS/tests
npm install
npx playwright test
```

A dedicated Docker Compose file (`docker-compose.test.yaml`) is available for spinning up a test environment.

